 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"b2bb5f92-b55d-43a5-9c27-862961056167"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next two elements are the atomic indices. transdd  considers only \
couplings between different atoms, in this case atoms 1 and 2. The fifth \
element is the coupling strength which carries the transition and atomic \
indices. The last element is the detuning between the two transitions. Note \
that when the two coupled transitions are the same, the detuning vanishes, \
i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Delta]", "1"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e4119773-b198-4c4b-8d4e-e29cf8249a18"],
 "  = 0. Conversely, when the transitions are different, the detuning is \
nonzero, i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Delta]", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c3fba1e5-9ce1-43a3-be19-9ed666c1f87a"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "1"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"005d5a11-ae94-426d-8433-c9e42c16b9e0"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"778fcc2d-c0ff-4070-b8fc-3f5ee7396006"],
 "-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "6"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"49377ca7-67cc-448c-9f62-2aa3d5776994"],
 "+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "7"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"4883e789-ea64-4363-ad68-9bfb776c4042"],
 ". In this case, the energy shifts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "1"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"5e8172b6-b85a-4636-b837-f5d714ecb325"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d9708006-c28d-4f96-8fb7-ea71281977f3"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]\[Epsilon]", "6"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"2334864e-d0b1-4f59-b6d0-ee3d5d60a4a5"],
