Cell[TextData[{
 "The first five entries of transLi list the decay channels between the \
states \[VerticalSeparator]1\[RightAngleBracket] and \[VerticalSeparator]2\
\[RightAngleBracket] ({1,2}) for each atom. These transitions occur \
internally within each atom, so the next two transition entries are (1, 1), \
(2, 2), (3, 3), (4, 4) and (5, 5) respectively indicating that each term \
involves only that specific atom. The parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "1"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d0a78d30-ad96-4680-8d87-ec82acc48492"],
 "corresponds to the decay rate of this transition. The last eight terms give \
rise to the collective channels formed between the transitions \
\[VerticalSeparator]1\[RightAngleBracket] \[RightArrow]  \
\[VerticalSeparator]2\[RightAngleBracket] between neighbouring atoms.  The \
parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6d176dc5-17dc-467f-ac5d-3f0338ade019"],
 " is collective decay rate of this kind of transition. The final 0  in each \
term transLi represents the energy difference between the two transitions. In \
this case, all these transitions are in fact the same, so the difference \
between the energy gaps is  zero."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9648713853636227`*^9, 3.964871796485074*^9}, {
   3.964871828723584*^9, 3.964871937190982*^9}, {3.964871989354904*^9, 
   3.964872030988288*^9}, {3.964872065116338*^9, 3.964872070272622*^9}, {
   3.964872118870276*^9, 3.964872142582684*^9}, {3.964872177723241*^9, 
   3.964872180762732*^9}, {3.9648722284812593`*^9, 3.964872247936729*^9}, {
   3.964872320249968*^9, 3.964872377279711*^9}, {3.964872529808708*^9, 
   3.964872541550843*^9}, {3.964879176062706*^9, 3.9648794120666428`*^9}, {
   3.9648794865149517`*^9, 3.9648795230729637`*^9}, {3.964879569113613*^9, 
   3.964879570198299*^9}, {3.964879812990485*^9, 3.964880020072877*^9}, {
